00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:42,480
Small, soft, pretty, weak.

283
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,380
(Quick review)
If it's me and Ding.

284
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:43,910
How do we choose?

285
00:08:43,910 --> 00:08:44,540
(He Da or Ding Dang)

286
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,880
Ding. He's younger.

287
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:48,900
What about the two of us being pretty?

288
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:50,660
(How do you choose?)

289
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:54,140
(Wants to hear both sides)
You two together.

290
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:55,980
(Unsure what to say)

291
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:57,320
We've hit a tough one.

292
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:58,440
(New bonus scenes)
How do we choose this?

293
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,020
(every Sunday at noon)

294
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:00,600
How would you guys choose?

295
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:02,680
Using your rule.

296
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:03,540
We...

297
00:09:04,020 --> 00:09:04,740
Well...

298
00:09:04,780 --> 00:09:05,580
(Starting to sweat)

299
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:08,160
He Da, please come in.

300
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:09,120
(Save He Da)
Go.

301
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:09,880
Go, He Da.

302
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:10,880
Have a seat.

303
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:15,700
(This round looks promising)

304
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:18,480
(What color pen will the next person use?)
Write down

305
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:20,200
(Ning 2K's answer: Red)
who do you think

306
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:22,960
is the bravest person in your group?

307
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:25,020
(Question is a distraction)

308
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:31,420
(Left hand)

309
00:09:31,660 --> 00:09:32,260
(Or right hand)

310
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:37,260
(I don't know)

311
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:39,900
(Randomly grabbed a black pen)

312
00:09:39,940 --> 00:09:42,140
(Oh no)

313
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,440
What if I forgot his name?

314
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:46,820
(Sincere)

315
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:48,500
(What kind of move is this?)

316
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:51,400
Then you can leave.

317
00:09:54,020 --> 00:09:56,540
(Brush flying across the page)

318
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:57,440
Are you done?

319
00:09:58,320 --> 00:09:58,760
Done.

320
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,500
(He Da's calligraphy showcase. Ke)

321
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:01,240
Thanks.

322
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:02,200
You can go now.

323
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:04,040
(Was that just a calligraphy showcase?)
I'm going out.

324
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:04,560
Everyone out.

325
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:05,680
Oh, everyone out.

326
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:11,700
(First test failed (1/4))

327
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:12,600
Wait.

328
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:14,600
We can't just use the rule, guys.

329
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:16,660
(We need a new strategy)

330
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:18,160
He asked what color

331
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,040
the second person would use.

332
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:19,800
I said red.

333
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:21,360
(Oh, now I get it)

334
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:22,160
I picked black.

335
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,040
(We discussed answers)
Didn't we agree on red?

336
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,120
We never said red.

337
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:26,440
Those two both picked red.

338
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,060
(Before the first test)
Red or yellow?

339
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:28,600
Red.

340
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:30,580
(Missed the discussion)

341
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,240
We were discussing red.

342
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:34,920
Yeah, but it's okay.

343
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:35,400
Look.

344
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:38,400
We'll stick with the classic rule.

345
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:40,320
(Notes 1. Small, soft, pretty, weak)
Everyone goes left first.

346
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:41,440
Left hand for everything.

347
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,160
(2. Left side goes first)
Everything is left.

348
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:43,760
Let's just pick one.

349
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:44,560
The guy will be me.

350
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:45,560
For the girl, let's pick one.

351
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:46,560
The girl will be Jin.

352
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:47,600
(3. Jin for girls, Ding for guys)
Okay.

353
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:48,560
For the color,

354
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:49,280
it'll be red.

355
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:49,800
(4. The color is red)

356
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:50,120
Okay.

357
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:50,640
Good.

358
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:53,380
(Second compatibility test begins)
The second test begins.

359
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:56,880
Player Jin Pretty, please come in alone.

360
00:10:58,040 --> 00:10:58,760
Jin Pretty.

361
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:00,760
Left.

362
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:01,560
Left, Jin.

363
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:04,220
(Taking back the right hand)

364
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:04,840
It's okay.

365
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:05,680
It's fine.

366
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:07,040
The first one's fine.

367
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:07,480
The second one.

368
00:11:07,760 --> 00:11:08,360
It starts with the second one.

369
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:11,880
I have three plates of snacks here.

370
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:13,960
Which one do you think

371
00:11:14,450 --> 00:11:16,040
the next person will eat first?

372
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:18,220
(Which snacks will the next person eat?)
The color is red.

373
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:20,100
(Choosing the red snacks)
This one.

374
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:20,480
Sure?

375
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:24,640
Player Nan Do, please come in alone.

376
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:26,480
Left.

377
00:11:26,620 --> 00:11:28,620
Small, soft, pretty, weak.

378
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:29,280
Left.

379
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:32,010
(Entering the test room)
Small, soft, pretty, weak.

380
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:32,600
Left.

381
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,240
Good morning.

382
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:36,200
Come on, have a seat.

383
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:38,040
(Which snacks will the next person eat?)
Have a snack.

384
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:39,400
(Jin Pretty's answer: the red snacks)

385
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:40,640
The color is red.

386
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:44,240
Is this okay?

387
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:45,980
(Choosing the red snacks)

388
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:47,020
(Great!)

389
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:48,920
How do you think the next person

390
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:51,440
will wink?

391
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:53,700
(How will the next person wink?)

392
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:54,740
(Both eyes tightly shut)
Like this.

393
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:56,360
She can't.

394
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:57,000
She can't do it.

395
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,800
(Nan Do can't wink)
You have to ask which eye.

396
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,160
I'll have to do it manually.

397
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:00,700
(Choosing a left-eye wink)

398
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:01,800
Left.

399
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:02,120
Yeah.

400
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:02,440
Yes.

401
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:02,720
Okay.

402
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:03,960
Now...

403
00:12:04,300 --> 00:12:05,200
(That's quite a surprise)

404
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:05,760
They passed.

405
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:07,040
Player He Da,

406
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:09,000
please come in alone.

407
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Left.

408
00:12:12,820 --> 00:12:14,860
(Left hand opens the door,
left foot goes in first)

409
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:18,340
(Left leg)

410
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:19,740
(Left leg first)

411
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:20,880
You need to greet the teacher.

412
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:22,180
(Mommy Nan is here)

413
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:23,480
Hi.

414
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:23,840
Hello.

415
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:24,960
Have a seat.

416
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:30,600
Please wink at me.

417
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:31,940
(How will the next person wink?)

418
00:12:31,940 --> 00:12:33,420
(Nan Do's answer: a left-eye wink)

419
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:35,700
(Chooses a left-eye wink)

420
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:36,200
Not bad.

421
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:41,760
Player Ke Cutie, please come in alone.

422
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:44,960
(Right hand opens the door)
Left hand closes the door.

423
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:46,380
(Smile disappears)

424
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:47,980
(Quick recovery)

425
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:51,060
(Ke Cutie's question: Confidential)

426
00:12:51,060 --> 00:12:52,620
(What does that mean?)

427
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:53,720
Have a seat.

428
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:55,140
(Paying close attention)

429
00:12:59,600 --> 00:12:59,880
Okay.

430
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:00,560
All set.

431
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:01,120
No problem now.

432
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:01,760
Next one can come in.

433
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:03,660
(What just happened?)

434
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:05,200
Do you think

435
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:06,680
the next person

436
00:13:06,680 --> 00:13:08,160
will touch the table?

437
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:10,980
(No)

438
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,120
(Absolutely sure)
He won't touch it.

439
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:12,880
Not once.

440
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:14,900
(Wait)

441
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:17,920
After he sits down,
his hand won't touch it?

442
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:19,920
After he sits down, right?

443
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:22,840
He will.

444
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:23,980
(Choosing yes)

445
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:26,240
Because this isn't about our rule.

446
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:27,000
Right.

447
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,080
It's just a physical reaction.

448
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,720
He'll definitely touch it.

449
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:31,720
(He really touched it)

450
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:32,920
I told you. It's a physical reaction.

451
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:34,620
(Only you could do that)

452
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:36,340
(The next question will be...)

453
00:13:39,900 --> 00:13:41,500
(Real test prop)

454
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:43,080
He asked what color

455
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:43,960
the second person would use.

456
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:44,800
I said red.

457
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:46,640
(This one's a sure thing)
What shape

458
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:49,520
will the next person draw?

459
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:51,180
(What shape will the next person draw?)

460
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:53,660
(We're doomed)

461
00:13:54,460 --> 00:13:58,100
(We never discussed this question)

462
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:01,160
I mean,

463
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:02,920
it's not asking what color, right?

464
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:03,620
(Ke wants the real test)

465
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,320
Our rule is all
about coming full circle.

466
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:07,520
I get it.

467
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:08,920
Because for a family,

468
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:11,400
the most important thing
is being together.

469
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:12,160
Right.

470
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,080
Right?

471
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:16,120
Okay.

472
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:19,540
(Choosing a circle)
How about this?

473
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:21,120
Draw a circle, roughly.

474
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:21,440
Okay.

475
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,320
Now,

476
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:26,880
player Ning 2K, please come in alone.

477
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:28,720
I'm the last one.

478
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:29,760
(This is so stressful)

479
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:31,000
Left.

480
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:31,440
It's okay.

481
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:39,000
Have a seat.

482
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:41,880
So many things.

483
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:42,540
(So much to look at)

484
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:44,800
Go ahead.

485
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:46,940
♪Round and round, round and round♪

486
00:14:46,940 --> 00:14:48,980
♪Day after day, year after year, me♪

487
00:14:48,980 --> 00:14:49,640
♪I look deeply into your face♪

488
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:50,520
Keep singing.

489
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:51,600
Come on. Very good.

490
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:53,040
(Trying hard to catch on)
Round and round, round and round.

491
00:14:53,040 --> 00:14:54,520
Round and round, round and round.

492
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:55,700
(Expression changed)
Get out.

493
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:56,400
You cheated.

494
00:14:57,700 --> 00:14:59,000
(How do we fix this?)
What?

495
00:14:59,000 --> 00:14:59,760
You didn't even ask a question.

496
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:01,000
Why did I cheat?

497
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,400
We were singing. I like singing.

498
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:04,480
(Just a hobby)
I like singing.

499
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:06,080
You never said we couldn't sing.

500
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:06,880
Exactly.

501
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:08,520
I know they were singing,
but that's their problem.

502
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:09,360
It has nothing to do with me.

503
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:10,800
You can't disqualify me.

504
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:12,200
I only get to take this test
once a year.

505
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:15,240
I totally understand.

506
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:15,800
I really do.

507
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:16,960
I understand how you feel.

508
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:17,640
Got it.

509
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:18,920
(Almost got away with it)

510
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:20,280
But I make the rules.

511
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:21,100
(Broke the no-talking, no-hints rule)
Get out.

512
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:21,280
Fine.

513
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:22,400
Okay.

514
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:23,960
Fine. I'll repeat a year next year.

515
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:24,840
Good. I'll be waiting.

516
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:26,560
Let's go back and repeat a year.

517
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:27,420
(Second test failed (2/4))

518
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:31,900
(Pressure: zero)

519
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:32,360
What happened?

520
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:33,480
He said we cheated.

521
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:35,000
Who knew he'd be that strict?

522
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,680
I gave him a signal
as soon as he came in.

523
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:36,960
Really?

524
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:37,880
I did this the moment he walked in.

525
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:38,240
Did you get it?

526
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:39,320
I didn't.

527
00:15:39,340 --> 00:15:40,780
(The hint was wasted too)

528
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:42,520
It's so hard. Really hard.

529
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:43,160
There's no way to predict it.

530
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:44,320
Actually, it's not that bad.

531
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,520
You guys already got through three.

532
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:46,480
But now we've actually

533
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:47,320
started to figure out the pattern.

534
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:48,760
What if he asks what song

535
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:50,440
the next person will sing?

536
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,160
Let the game of reason start.

537
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,600
(Notes 5. Theme Song)
Let the game of reason start.

538
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:55,440
And what character will they write?

539
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:56,840
What character?

540
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:57,640
Write "small".

541
00:15:57,640 --> 00:15:59,330
(6. Write "small")
Small, soft, pretty, weak. Small.

542
00:15:59,360 --> 00:15:59,880
Got it.

543
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:01,400
Okay, I think we've got this one.

544
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:01,720
Let's do it.

545
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:02,200
(Overflowing with confidence)
Really?

546
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:02,720
Okay, come on.

547
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:06,840
(Third compatibility test begins)
Ding Dang, please come in alone.

548
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:08,880
Have a seat.

549
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:13,160
I have these sticky notes here.

550
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:15,160
What body part

551
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:19,120
will the next person stick it on?

552
00:16:19,180 --> 00:16:20,800
(What body part
will the next person stick it on?)

553
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:21,600
Why are you laughing?

554
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:22,880
You didn't expect this?

555
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:23,960
(Got hit by the sticky notes)

556
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:24,720
Didn't expect it to be this one, huh?

557
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:27,920
(Notes: 1. Small, soft, pretty, weak.
2. Left comes first)

558
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:28,710
(3. Jin Pretty comes first.
4. Color: red)

559
00:16:28,730 --> 00:16:29,660
(5. Theme song. 6. Write small)

560
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:30,960
Which body part?

561
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:32,720
Pick a body part.

562
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:33,000
I...

563
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:34,720
(Chooses the back of the left hand)

564
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:35,520
Put it

565
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:36,160
