2847
01:24:35,800 --> 01:24:36,780
(Wu Zhihong, Renowned Psychologist, Founder of Seeing Counseling Center)
Because this kind of encouragement

2848
01:24:36,780 --> 01:24:37,680
(Author of more than 10 psychology books)
is essentially

2849
01:24:37,680 --> 01:24:38,120
(People often encourage us to cheer up.)
a form of invalidating

2850
01:24:38,120 --> 01:24:40,360
(Why can encouragement sometimes cause more harm instead?)
what someone is going through

2851
01:24:40,360 --> 01:24:41,600
when they're in a traumatized emotional state.

2852
01:24:41,600 --> 01:24:42,960
We experience the world
through our feelings.

2853
01:24:43,360 --> 01:24:45,240
And those emotions and feelings

2854
01:24:45,240 --> 01:24:47,400
are very real
to the person experiencing them.

2855
01:24:47,400 --> 01:24:48,920
If we simply tell them,

2856
01:24:48,920 --> 01:24:50,320
"You need to look on the bright side,"

2857
01:24:50,320 --> 01:24:51,360
or something similar...

2858
01:24:51,360 --> 01:24:52,920
Even the phrase "look on
the bright side" is telling them

2859
01:24:52,920 --> 01:24:54,600
to use their thoughts

2860
01:24:54,600 --> 01:24:57,120
to deny and shut down

2861
01:24:57,120 --> 01:24:57,960
what they're experiencing.

2862
01:24:57,960 --> 01:24:59,640
So at that point, the person may feel

2863
01:25:00,040 --> 01:25:02,640
that their experience
is being invalidated.

2864
01:25:02,640 --> 01:25:03,760
And that can further

2865
01:25:03,760 --> 01:25:05,480
increase their sense of shame.

2866
01:25:05,480 --> 01:25:06,560
This may lead

2867
01:25:06,560 --> 01:25:08,600
to further psychological problems

2868
01:25:08,600 --> 01:25:09,320
and, in severe cases,

2869
01:25:09,320 --> 01:25:10,680
even mental disorders.

2870
01:25:10,960 --> 01:25:11,800
(If someone around us is experiencing depression, anxiety, or trauma,)
when they're in that state,

2871
01:25:11,800 --> 01:25:12,920
(what should we do?)
I think first of all,

2872
01:25:12,920 --> 01:25:14,200
as someone supporting them,

2873
01:25:14,200 --> 01:25:14,920
you also need to be careful

2874
01:25:14,920 --> 01:25:15,360
not to get pulled

2875
01:25:15,360 --> 01:25:16,600
into their emotional state yourself.

2876
01:25:16,600 --> 01:25:17,480
So I think

2877
01:25:17,480 --> 01:25:18,840
it's important
to maintain basic boundaries.

2878
01:25:18,840 --> 01:25:20,560
Beyond that, if you're able to,

2879
01:25:20,560 --> 01:25:22,760
empathy can
of course be incredibly helpful.

2880
01:25:22,840 --> 01:25:24,600
We can listen to what they have to say

2881
01:25:24,600 --> 01:25:26,560
and try to understand

2882
01:25:26,560 --> 01:25:29,240
what they're feeling.

2883
01:25:29,560 --> 01:25:30,480
Although I'm not you,

2884
01:25:30,480 --> 01:25:31,320
I can still try to understand

2885
01:25:31,320 --> 01:25:32,920
how you're feeling.

2886
01:25:32,920 --> 01:25:34,720
That makes a huge difference.

2887
01:25:34,720 --> 01:25:36,960
Of course, if empathy
doesn't come naturally to you,

2888
01:25:37,240 --> 01:25:39,160
or you're not particularly good at it,

2889
01:25:39,160 --> 01:25:40,040
then simply being there

2890
01:25:40,040 --> 01:25:42,960
can be a wonderful gift.

2891
01:25:42,960 --> 01:25:45,280
I allow you to stay here,

2892
01:25:45,280 --> 01:25:46,920
and I'll stay here with you,

2893
01:25:46,920 --> 01:25:48,160
patiently.

2894
01:25:48,160 --> 01:25:50,000
For ordinary people,

2895
01:25:50,000 --> 01:25:51,520
this is a very good way

2896
01:25:51,520 --> 01:25:52,960
we can use to support someone.

2897
01:25:52,960 --> 01:25:55,020
(Seeing their emotions and embracing their feelings
can itself be a form of healing.)

2898
